\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, all whoe'er have set
\par Your faces Zion-ward,
\par In Jesus let us meet,
\par And praise our common Lord;
\par In Jesus let us still go on,
\par Till all appear before His throne.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Nearer, and near still,
\par We to our country come,
\par To that celestial hill,
\par The weary pilgrim's home:
\par The new Jerusalem above,
\par The seat of everlasting love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The peace and joy of faith
\par Each moment may we feel;
\par Redeemed from sin and wrath,
\par From earth, and death, and hell,
\par We to our Father's house repair,
\par To meet our elder Brother there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Our Brother, Saviour, Head,
\par Our all in all, is He;
\par And in His steps who tread
\par We soon His face shall see;
\par Shall see Him with our glorious friends,
\par And then in heaven our journey ends.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

